.TH GLASSOSD 1 "2026-08-29" "glassosd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glassosd \- unified notification daemon, OSD and control centre
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glassosd
.SH DESCRIPTION
A single daemon replacing four Plasma shell surfaces with one consistent
design: notification popups, the volume and brightness OSD, the lock\-key
indicators, and a notification centre.
.PP
It implements
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
and so replaces whatever notification server was serving that name. Normally
started by its systemd user unit or on demand by D\-Bus activation, rather than
run by hand.
.PP
Configuration lives in
.BR glassosdrc (5)
and is driven at runtime by
.BR glassosdctl (1).
.SH MODULES
Each half runs independently, and off means never constructed \(em no bus name,
no Wayland surface, no watchers. Modules are read at startup.
.TP
.B notifications
The notification server and its popups.
.TP
.B centre
The control centre and tray icon.
.TP
.B osd
Volume, brightness and media OSD.
.TP
.B lockkeys
Caps, num and Fn lock indicators.
.PP
.nf
glassosdctl module
glassosdctl module osd off
glassosdctl restart
.fi
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A compositor implementing
.BR wlr\-layer\-shell\-unstable\-v1 :
KDE Plasma, Hyprland, sway, river, Wayfire, labwc and other wlroots\-based
compositors. It does not work on GNOME, which does not implement layer\-shell,
nor on X11.
.PP
Compositor blur is optional. Without it, glass surfaces close up automatically
rather than being merely see\-through; see
.B Solidity
in
.BR glassosdrc (5).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Saves history and snooze state, then exits.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/glassosdrc
Configuration; see
.BR glassosdrc (5).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/glassosd/history.json
Notification history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/glassosd/snoozed.json
Snoozed notifications and their wake times.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.nf
glassosdctl status
journalctl \-\-user \-u glassosd \-f
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glassosdctl (1),
.BR glassosdrc (5),
.BR notify\-send (1)
.SH AUTHORS
The glassosd contributors.
